  "raw": {
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Director-of-the-Center-for-Disability-and-Accommodations_R936": {
      "title": "Director of the Center for Disability and Accommodations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Director of the Center for Disability & Accommodations Position : Western Colorado University invites applications for an in-person, full-time position of Director of the Center for Disability & Accommodations (CDA).  The position reports to the Office of the Provost. Candidate has a demonstrated track record of stakeholder relationship-building as well as excellent organizational and interpersonal skills.  The position provides strategic leadership for the CDA while innovating and managing all student accommodation services through a student-centered framework and a campuswide collaborative approach.  Ensures the CDA’s compliance with university policies as well as state and federal laws related to disability, accessibility, and accommodations. Responsibilities: Student Accommodation and Support Services: Develops, implements, and oversees comprehensive student accommodation services.  Oversees the interactive process workflow; maintains an active caseload; ensures timely and accurate accommodation review, reasonable determination, and record keeping in line with ADA/504 best practices; regularly collaborates with Residence Life on housing and dining accommodations; oversees student classroom support services including assistive technologies; coordinates standardized exams (GRE, ACT, etc.); reviews and makes initial determinations regarding student appeals & grievances. Internal and External Collaboration: Mentors and guides CDA staff in ADA/504 best practices; Builds and maintains meaningful partnerships across campus and with community stakeholders; works closely and collaboratively with students, faculty, and staff to implement educational strategies that support accessibility and inclusion, including Admissions, The Teaching and Learning Center, Facilities, and Student Affairs; keeps current in the field through active involvement in regional and national networks related to disability services in higher education; serves on university committees as needed. Training and Consultation: Collaborates with Access and Testing Center Coordinator and other campus offices in designing and delivering professional training to improve campus understanding of disability, accessibility, and accommodations; provides advice to faculty and staff to promote inclusive practices and an equitable learning environment. Budget and Planning: Manages the CDA’s operational budget; leads program assessment efforts to measure outcomes and inform continuous improvement of services.  Maintains and regularly updates the CDA Standard Operating Procedures, ensuring ongoing operational alignment and consistent practices. Legal Compliance: Maintains current knowledge of and ensuring CDA compliance with university policies and state and federal law related to disability, accessibility, and accommodations.  Completes annual reporting as required by the state. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Behavioral Health, Social Work, Counseling, Human Resources, Special Education, or related field, or will have earned this degree within the first 12 months of the position start date. Three years of progressive experience providing accessibility and accommodation services in a university or educational setting. Three years of supervisory experience. Demonstrated knowledge of ADA/504 and FERPA regulations. Exceptional and demonstrated collaborative skills/ability to build and maintain partnerships. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to detail. Project management experience from ideation through completion. Proficiency with Microsoft Office suite Preferred Qualifications: Experience using Workday and AIM platforms. Understanding of inclusive pedagogy. Three or more years supervisory experience of non-student professional staff. Compensation: $65,000 - $70,000 annually.  This position is FLSA exempt.   Western offers an excellent benefits package including shared premiums for a comprehensive health insurance plan, dental insurance, retirement plan, life insurance, and other insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for dependents enrolled full time in undergraduate programs for up to four years. Application Procedure:  Apply online at www.Western.edu/jobs . Candidates must submit the following: Resume or CV; letter of interest addressing how experiences/qualifications connect with the required/preferred characteristics and priorities as expressed in this position profile; contact information for three references. In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information. Unfortunately, Western Colorado University cannot sponsor a visa for this position at this time. Please direct questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Kelsey Bennett, at kbennett@western.edu. Application deadline is October 15, 2026. Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university. Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy in skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District . An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Bus-Driver--Part-time_R120": {
      "title": "Bus Driver, Part-time",
      "description": "Start date: 2023-05-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPosition Summary: Part-time, as-needed CDL driver for Western Colorado University Athletics Department. Must have Class B CDL with passenger endorsement, no air-brake restriction & an excellent driving record. $35/hour up to 6 hours or $350/day + per diem. Job Description: Western seeks a bus driver with a current CDL for part-time, as-needed work for Western Colorado University Athletics Department. Duties: Transport Western Athletes to competitions in Colorado and throughout the west. Safely and confidently operate 56-passenger motor-coach or 30-passenger shuttle bus in a variety of weather conditions including rain, ice and snow over mountainous roads. Must be available for overnight trips and late night returns to Gunnison. Must work with coaching staff to deal with any changes or interruptions in trip itinerary. Conducts vehicle pre-trip and post trip inspections and complies with Western's vehicle services policies and procedures. Minimum Qualifications : Must have current Colorado Class B CDL with passenger endorsement, no air-brake restriction & an excellent driving record. Employment is subject to successful previous employer record check, department of motor vehicle record check, FMCSA drug and alcohol clearinghouse query, and pre-employment drug screening. Compensation: $35/hour up to 6 hours or $350/day + per diem. Benefits include PERA retirement plan participation, discounted Western fitness center membership, admission to athletic events for which duties are performed. How to apply: complete our online application. After the Bus Driver Manager reviews online application, you will need to complete a full bus driver application packet (to be supplied by the manager). Contact Joe Spillyards -- Athletics Vehicle Manager - 970.759.9592 with questions. Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 graduate and undergraduate students, the majority of which reside on the campus and in the community.  With average class sizes of 17 students, faculty and staff share a strong commitment to inclusivity and personalized, immersive education. They are student-oriented, collegial, enthusiastic, and engaged in the campus and community. Western is committed to continual growth in regard to diversity, equity, and inclusivity and promotes participation in DEI initiatives from students, faculty, staff, and the community. Please see our  diversity statement , and our  DEI Committee charge . The University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, a rural community 200 miles southwest of Denver and the gateway to Crested Butte, a world class ski community.  K-12 students are served by the award-winning  Gunnison Watershed School District . Both communities value the arts, quality of life, community-based wrap around services for children and adults, and continued personal growth and learning opportunities. At an elevation of 7,700 feet in the southern Rocky Mountains, the Gunnison Valley provides exceptional year-round outdoor recreational and cultural opportunities including summer arts and music festivals, mountain biking, skiing, kayak/rafting, rock climbing, hiking and camping… all within minutes of the campus. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university. Western Colorado University believes that equity, diversity, and inclusion drive our success, and we encourage candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. Western is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy, medical condition related to pregnancy, creed, ancestry, national origin, marital status, genetic information, or military status (for state classified positions, with preference given to military veterans), or any other protected status in accordance with applicable law. Please see our diversity statement, and our DEII Committee charge.   ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS"
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Tenure-Track-Faculty-in-Art-and-Design_R944": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty in Art and Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: The School of the Arts at Western Colorado University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Art and Design. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar who is committed to student-centered learning, professional preparation, and inclusive, interdisciplinary education. This is an in-person, on-campus position on our vibrant residential campus in Gunnison, Colorado.   The standard teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year.  The successful candidate will deliver engaging, well-designed Art and Design courses, including introductory courses in Art and Design, as well as introductory and advanced courses (Drawing, 2D/3D Design, Sculpture, Digital Design, and Magazine Production). Additionally they may teach other courses aligned with their expertise and departmental needs. We especially value faculty who engage students in high-impact practices such as internships, research, community-based learning, and who participate in our Western Watershed General Education and First-Year Seminar Headwaters courses. We value faculty who work to prepare students for a livelihood based on their values and aid students in gaining post-graduate opportunities.    The recently launched School of the Arts at Western serves approximately 160 students enrolled across six disciplines: art, design, film, music, industrial design, and theatre. It also provides substantial service to the Western Watershed program.   Learn more about Western’s School of the Arts here: https://western.edu/department/school-of-the-arts/                                     Please note: Western is unable to sponsor work authorization for this position.   QUALIFICATIONS:       Minimum qualifications: An MFA or PhD in Art, Graphic Design, or closely related field; ABD would also be considered.  Candidates must have a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate education, excellence in teaching, and willingness to work with and be sensitive to the educational needs of all students.  Candidates must also be able to use technology in instructional delivery, including ability to teach online and hybrid courses. Collegiality and professional flexibility are sought in the successful candidate.   Preferred qualifications: Preference given to candidates with 3 years full time teaching experience in Art or Design Professional and/or teaching experience in art foundation courses (2D, 3D, Drawing, Design) Professional or college teaching experience in sculpture Professional or college teaching experience in Graphic Design courses (Digital Design and Magazine Production) Interest in interdisciplinary and innovative curriculum development and teaching To be considered for the Associate level, applicants must demonstrate experience with program administration and growth, curriculum development, recruitment, retention, advising, and experience with developing professional/industry partnerships for student internships and career connections. Further, preference will be given to applicants with these experiences in addition to their professional art making experience.     SALARY/BENEFITS:  $55,000-$58,000 (Assistant Professor) or $65,000 - $68,000 (Associate Professor) annualized salary. Western offers an excellent benefits package including shared premiums for a comprehensive health insurance plan, dental insurance, retirement plan, life insurance, and other insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for dependents enrolled full time in undergraduate programs for up to four years.    START DATE:  August 16, 2027   APPLICATION:  Apply online at www.western.edu/jobs .  Required attachments to the application include: letter of application, curriculum vitae, evidence of successful teaching and mentoring ( a portfolio of 20 images of student artwork), evidence of successful scholarly or creative activity (personal artwork portfolio of 20 images), and a reference list with names and contact information of three references, including one from a current supervisor.                                     In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.   Please direct questions to Tina Butterfield at (970) 943-2008; email: tbutterfield@western.edu.    APPLICATION DEADLINE: November 10, 2026. Screening of applications will begin immediately.     Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university. Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy in skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District . Western Colorado University encourages candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. Western is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants in accordance with applicable law.   An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets.       WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Assistant-Professor-of-Music_R945": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Western Colorado University invites applications for a full-time, Assistant Professor of Music, with a specialization in Choir and Music Education. We seek a dynamic teacher-scholar who is committed to student-centered learning, professional preparation, and inclusive, interdisciplinary education. This is an in-person, on-campus position on our vibrant residential campus in Gunnison, Colorado. The standard teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year. The successful candidate will deliver engaging, well-designed instruction for our vocal ensembles and will teach other courses aligned with their expertise and discipline needs. This position organizes and delivers the annual Western Slope Honor Choir as a service duty. We especially value faculty who engage students in high-impact practices such as internships, research, community-based learning, and who participate in our Western Watershed General Education and First-Year Seminar Headwaters courses. We value faculty who work to prepare students for a livelihood based on their values and aid students in gaining post-graduate opportunities.   The Music Program resides within the new School of the Arts at Western, which serves approximately 160 students enrolled across six disciplines: art, design, film, music, industrial design, and theatre. It also provides substantial service to the Western Watershed program. Students can earn a BA degree in Music Education (with K-12 licensure), Music Industry, or Music Performance; combining rigorous academic preparation with high-impact experiential learning.   Learn more about the Music Program at: www.western.edu/music Learn more about the School of the Arts at: https://western.edu/department/school-of-the-arts/   Please note: Western is unable to sponsor work authorization for this position.   QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications: A DMA or other terminal degree with an emphasis in Music is required; ABD also considered for appointment. Candidates must have a demonstrated commitment to undergraduate education, excellence in teaching, and willingness to work with and be sensitive to the educational needs of all students. Candidates must also be able to use technology in instructional delivery, including the ability to teach online and hybrid courses. Collegiality and professional flexibility are sought in the successful candidate. Preferred Qualifications: Choir direction at the collegiate level is preferred; candidates with public school choir direction will be considered. Undergraduate teaching experience in music education pedagogy courses is preferred; candidates with public school teaching experience in music will be considered. Undergraduate teaching experience in music theory, aural skills, class piano, instrumental lessons, voice lessons, and/or music history is preferred.   SALARY/BENEFITS:  $55,000-$58,000 annualized salary. Western offers an excellent benefits package including shared premiums for a comprehensive health insurance plan, dental insurance, retirement plan, life insurance, and other insurance options. After one year of employment, Western provides free tuition for dependents enrolled full time in undergraduate programs for up to four years. START DATE:  August 16, 2027   APPLICATION:  Apply online at www.western.edu/jobs .  Required attachments to the application include: letter of application detailing how you meet the required and preferred qualifications, curriculum vitae, a document with links to video of choral performances and/or rehearsal they have directed, and a reference list with names and contact information of three references, including one from a current supervisor. Optionally, ca ndidates may submit a document with links to video of their own vocal or instrumental performance.                                     In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.   Please direct questions to the search chair Ben Justis at: bjustis@western.edu   APPLICATION DEADLINE:  November 1, 2026. Screening of applications will begin immediately.   Additional Information on Western and Gunnison/Crested Butte Western Colorado University is a public institution with an enrollment of ~3,700 students. 47% of students are undergraduates, 33% are graduate students, and 80% receive some form of financial aid. Western students represent 17 countries, 50 states, and almost every county in Colorado. With an average class size of 17, Western’s faculty and staff share a strong commitment to personalized, rigorous, and immersive education. Visit  http://www.western.edu  to learn more about the university. Western Colorado University is located in Gunnison, Colorado, about 200 miles southwest of Denver amidst over 2 million acres of public land and a vibrant ranching community. The Gunnison valley provides robust cultural programming and exceptional outdoor recreation. A network of dedicated community organizations enrich the lives of many in the tight-knit community. Living in the valley , one appreciates a vibrant culture of festivals, exhibitions, performances, wellness activities, and more. In the winter, many enjoy skiing at Crested Butte Mountain Resort and along dozens of miles of cross-country trails. In the summer, bikers, hikers, and runners explore 750-plus miles of singletrack trails, while others delight in fishing, boating, and paddleboarding at Blue Mesa Reservoir or on the Gunnison River and its tributaries. Pre-K-12 students are served by the highly-ranked Gunnison Watershed School District . Western Colorado University encourages qualified candidates from all identities, backgrounds, and abilities to apply. Western is an equal opportunity employer committed to building inclusive, innovative work environments with employees who reflect our communities and enthusiastically serve them. Therefore, in all aspects of the employment process, we provide employment opportunities to all qualified applicants in accordance with applicable law.   An Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/vets. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
    },
    "https://western.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/WESTERN/job/Gunnison-CO/Associate-Provost_R947": {
      "title": "Associate Provost",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-09\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Summary: Job Description: Western Colorado University is seeking an Associate Provost to help shape the future of academic excellence, innovation, and student success in Gunnison, Colorado. Reporting directly to the Provost, this senior leader will influence undergraduate and graduate education, faculty development, strategic initiatives, and institutional priorities, including oversight of the School of Graduate Studies and a campuswide general education reform initiative. This is an on-campus opportunity for a collaborative, forward-thinking academic leader ready to make a university-wide impact. To view the full job announcement and apply, please go to the Another Source website: Associate Provost Do NOT click the \"apply\" button on this screen. All applications must be submitted to Another Source at the link above. WESTERN COLORADO UNIVERSITY IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER INCLUDING DISABILITY/VETERANS It is the ongoing policy and practice of Western Colorado University to provide equal opportunity in employment to all employees and applicants.  No person shall be discriminated against in any condition of employment because of age (40 and over), color, disability, gender identity, genetic information, military or veteran status, national origin, ancestry, race, religion, creed, sex, sexual orientation, gender expression, marital status, or any other applicable status protected by federal, state, or local law. ADAAA ACCOMMODATIONS: Western Colorado University is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Western will assist individuals who have a disability with any reasonable accommodation requests related to employment, including completing the application process, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, participating in the employee selection process, and/or performing essential job functions where the requested accommodation does not impose an undue hardship. If you have a disability and require reasonable accommodation to ensure you have a positive experience applying or interviewing for this position, please direct your inquiries to the Office of Human Resources at HR@western.edu or (970) 943-3140."
